Package: vale
Architecture: amd64
Depends:
 ${misc:Depends},
Description: syntax-aware linter for prose
 Vale checks prose against style rules: packaged guides such as Microsoft's
 and Google's, or a project's own rules in .vale.ini and a styles directory.
 It understands Markdown, reStructuredText, AsciiDoc, HTML, and the comments
 and docstrings of most programming languages, so code stays out of the way
 of the prose checks.
 .
 This package repacks the upstream release binary, a static Go build: no
 Ubuntu or Debian archive carries vale, and upstream publishes tarballs
 only. debian/rules downloads the release named in debian/changelog and
 checks it against the sha256 recorded in debian/upstream-sha256.
